 "note": [
  "Thomas weaves Scripture into his sentences, usually from the Latin Vulgate and almost never with a reference. Swahili has no reachable public-domain Union Version text that matches the shipped corpus, so verse wording was mined from SHIPPED *.sw.json files (an aligned en↔sw corpus) and pasted verbatim where Thomas quotes a verse the way the Union Version reads it; mined rows cite the file. Where Thomas follows the Vulgate, re-persons a verse, or quotes a fragment the corpus does not carry, it is rendered in Union register and marked self_rendered.",
  "AI-translated (job #7642) in fifteen parallel chapter ranges against one shared term table, then reconciled. Divine free pronouns are capitalized (Wewe, Yeye, Mimi for Christ in Books III–IV), possessive stems lower case, as in the shipped sw corpus. Allusions that are not quotations carry no row. Awaiting native review."
